fr:mainmatter.html:p:
Both recursive holes sit under a literal, so F is locally
contractive and (S,T) = μ F exists. Derivatives strip the guard and
return the sibling undifferentiated (Step 2):

fr:mainmatter.html:ul:
ε ⟹ true; ⊥, char a ⟹ false;

_·_ ⟹ conjunction;

_⊕_ ⟹ disjunction;

_* ⟹ true;

μ ⟹ decide on the body under a freshly nullable
    recursive occurrence; the productivity side condition from
    CFGDesc makes this terminating.

